# Distribution boundary: what a consumer gets under vendor/.
#
# Allowlist, not blocklist, and deliberately so: with a blocklist every new top-level
# file ships silently until someone remembers to exclude it.
#
# Both lines per directory are required. Measured, not assumed: `export-ignore` on a
# directory prunes the whole subtree, so unsetting only `/src/**` yields an archive
# without src/ at all, and unsetting only `/src` yields an empty src/ directory.
#
# Verify with the build, never by reading this file:
#     git archive HEAD | tar t

* export-ignore

/src            -export-ignore
/src/**         -export-ignore
/stubs          -export-ignore
/stubs/**       -export-ignore
/bin            -export-ignore
/bin/**         -export-ignore
# ci/ is opened by the single file the documentation tells a consumer to run
# (docs/DX_GUIDE.md, "Local DBMS"), not by `/ci/**`: naming the file keeps the allowlist
# property — a future ci/ file does not ship until it is listed here on purpose.
/ci             -export-ignore
/ci/docker-compose.yml -export-ignore
/bootstrap.php  -export-ignore
/composer.json  -export-ignore
/LICENSE        -export-ignore
/README.md      -export-ignore
/README.ru.md   -export-ignore
